spice-widget: a transparent color

WinBoat's seamless app windows show a part of the guest's screen, so the guest's desktop shows around and through
them: rounded corners, see-through windows. With the guest's desktop in one color that apps don't use, leaving out
that color's pixels shows the host's desktop there instead.

- spice_display_set_transparent_color() leaves out the pixels of a color (OpenGL drawing: the fragment shader
  discards them, over a transparent clear).
- SPICE_GTK_EGL_ALPHA picks an EGL config with an alpha channel and a 32-bit visual (X11), set before displays are
  created: the config is chosen when a display is. The guest's alpha means nothing: the picture is drawn opaque
  (the cursor keeps its alpha).

